# ntdll: Add support for pseudo environment variables __APPDIR__ and __CD__
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11530 state=closed
# implements support for the `__APPDIR__`  and `__CD__`  pseudo environment variables, which are available system-wide on Windows via `GetEnvironmentVariable`.

They are available system-wide, not just in cmd.exe.

Based on Eric Pouech's original patches from [Bug 52544](https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=52544)

Apart from the patches: 

* Rebased onto current tree
* Added const qualifiers to the static name arrays and pointer in `ENV_get_pseudo_variable`
* Replaced `++ptr` with `ptr + 1` to avoid mutating the pointer
* Renamed `len` → `dirlen` in the `__APPDIR__` path to avoid shadowing the function parameter
* Simplified the buffer length check from `(len + 1) * sizeof(WCHAR)` to `*ret_len + sizeof(WCHAR)`
* Updated format specifiers in tests from `%x` to `%#lx` to match the surrounding test file conventions

Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=52544 

Co-authored-by: Eric Pouech eric.pouech@gmail.com
